  "description": "The emotion of concern is expressed through the visual depiction of a massive, overwhelming pile of trash dominating the landscape, combined with the textual overlay 'so much trash' and 'we need a garbage collector.' The image and text together evoke a sense of alarm and urgency regarding environmental degradation and the failure of waste management systems. The sheer scale of pollution visually communicates distress, while the text explicitly calls for action, reinforcing the emotional weight of the situation.",
